1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,080
You can do the same exact thing on that left leg.

2
00:00:03,080 --> 00:00:04,640
Start with a smaller range of motion.

3
00:00:04,640 --> 00:00:06,200
Start working it bigger and bigger and bigger

4
00:00:06,200 --> 00:00:07,800
as you feel more comfortable with it.

5
00:00:07,800 --> 00:00:10,220
Again, reaching across with that right hand this time,

6
00:00:10,220 --> 00:00:12,000
down to that left foot, trying to get that torso

7
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:13,400
to rotate just a little bit.

8
00:00:20,660 --> 00:00:22,320
And just 10 seconds left.

9
00:00:22,320 --> 00:00:23,840
We're gonna switch to this next exercise here

10
00:00:23,840 --> 00:00:24,960
in just a second.

11
00:00:24,960 --> 00:00:26,920
We're gonna be doing a knee up rotation.

12
00:00:26,920 --> 00:00:28,860
It's a relatively slow motion.

13
00:00:28,900 --> 00:00:32,140
Switch over in two seconds and switch it.

14
00:00:32,140 --> 00:00:34,360
So those knees are gonna be coming up really nice and high.

15
00:00:34,360 --> 00:00:36,660
Bring that opposite elbow down to that opposite knee,

16
00:00:36,660 --> 00:00:38,660
rotating those shoulders as much as you can.

17
00:00:38,660 --> 00:00:40,060
You want to actually feel like you're trying

18
00:00:40,060 --> 00:00:43,100
to get that elbow to the outside of your knee.

19
00:00:43,100 --> 00:00:45,180
You want to really focus on driving that knee up

20
00:00:45,180 --> 00:00:47,340
nice and high as well as rotating those shoulders

21
00:00:47,340 --> 00:00:48,940
as much as you possibly can.

22
00:00:48,940 --> 00:00:51,220
Get as much range of motion out of this possible

23
00:00:51,220 --> 00:00:52,340
and keep breathing normally.

24
00:00:52,340 --> 00:00:53,460
You got about 10 seconds left

25
00:00:53,460 --> 00:00:55,220
till we switch to the next exercise,

26
00:00:55,220 --> 00:00:57,660
which is gonna be a squat with a toe touch kick.

27
00:00:58,860 --> 00:01:01,140
Just a couple seconds left.

